.\" Verium testnet manual page
.TH VERIUM-TESTNET "1" "February 2025" "Verium 1.3.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
verium-testnet \- guide to using the Verium test network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B veriumd \-testnet
.br
.B verium-qt \-testnet
.br
.B verium-cli \-testnet
.I <command>
.br
.B verium-tx \-testnet
.I <command>
.br
.B verium-wallet \-testnet
.I <command>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verium supports a public test network (testnet) for development and testing without
using real VRM. Testnet is enabled in Verium 1.3.5.2 and onward.
.PP
Testnet uses separate network parameters, a different blockchain, and test-only coins
that have no real-world value. This allows developers and users to experiment with
wallets, transactions, and mining without risk.
.SH USAGE
.SS Starting in testnet mode
To use testnet, add the
.B \-testnet
(or
.BR \-chain=test )
flag when starting any Verium component:
.PP
.B veriumd \-testnet
.RS
Start the Verium daemon on testnet. Data is stored in
.I ~/.verium/testnet3
(see
.BR \-datadir ).
.RE
.PP
.B verium-qt \-testnet
.RS
Start the Verium GUI wallet on testnet. The window title will indicate "testnet"
to avoid confusion with mainnet.
.RE
.PP
.B verium-cli \-testnet getblockchaininfo
.RS
Query the testnet node via RPC. You must run
.B veriumd \-testnet
first, or specify
.B \-rpcconnect
to connect to a remote testnet node.
.RE
.SS Configuration file
Add to your
.I verium.conf
(in the appropriate datadir):
.PP
.B testnet=1
.PP
Or use a testnet-specific config:
.PP
.B veriumd \-datadir=\fI~/.verium/testnet3\fR \-conf=verium-testnet.conf
.PP
With
.I verium-testnet.conf
containing:
.B testnet=1
.SH NETWORK PARAMETERS
.TP
.B P2P port
36989 (mainnet uses 36988)
.TP
.B RPC port
33988 (mainnet uses 33987)
.TP
.B Data directory
.I ~/.verium/testnet3
(by default, when using
.B \-testnet
with default datadir)
.TP
.B Address prefixes
Testnet uses different address version bytes; addresses are not interchangeable
between mainnet and testnet.
.SH OBTAINING TEST COINS AND BOOTSTRAP
Testnet VRM has no value. For information on obtaining testnet coins, bootstrap
data, or other testnet resources, reach out in the Verium communication portal
(e.g. Telegram) or check the project wiki (https://docs.vericonomy.com).
.PP
Do not use mainnet addresses or wallets with testnet. Always keep mainnet and
testnet data separate.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
All Verium commands support
.B \-testnet
and
.BR \-chain=test .
They are equivalent.
.PP
When using
.BR verium-cli ,
.BR verium-tx ,
or
.BR verium-wallet ,
you must pass
.B \-testnet
if your daemon or node is running on testnet, so the client connects to the
correct RPC port (33988).
